This is the theory that uses the Greek letter phi

43:00.160 --> 43:05.600
to mathematically measure consciousness based on how integrated a network is.

43:05.960 --> 43:09.620
IIT is a brilliant measure of instantaneous integration.

43:10.240 --> 43:15.240
It calculates how tightly the different parts of a system constrain each other at a specific moment in time.

43:15.840 --> 43:18.020
But Fliction points out the fatal flaw.

43:18.100 --> 43:18.660
Which is...

43:18.660 --> 43:21.220
A system can have a massive phi value.

43:21.220 --> 43:28.740
It can be incredibly highly integrated, but still be structurally, globally reversible.

43:29.080 --> 43:32.560
So IIT successfully measures the complexity of the state,

43:32.880 --> 43:36.340
but worldhood measures the irreversibility of the history.

43:36.640 --> 43:36.880
Right.

43:36.880 --> 43:43.100
You could engineer a highly integrated artificial neural network that scores off the charts on phi,

43:43.700 --> 43:48.080
but if you can still hit a reset switch and perfectly restore its previous weights,

43:48.340 --> 43:50.100
it fails the groupoid test.

43:50.600 --> 43:53.660
It's an integrated simulation, but still a simulation.

43:53.860 --> 43:54.300
What's next?

43:54.520 --> 43:55.260
Assembly theory.

43:55.600 --> 43:55.880
Yes.

43:56.120 --> 43:56.800
Assembly theory.

