against an internal generative model of the outside world.

45:31.800 --> 45:34.180
It deeply involves history and survival.

45:34.400 --> 45:35.600
But where does it fall short?

45:36.000 --> 45:39.520
It falls short because it remains fundamentally inferential.

45:39.520 --> 45:48.200
Unless that generative model's history physically and irreversibly binds the system's future computational capacity,

45:48.880 --> 45:53.480
unless the system is physically degraded or permanently altered by the Bayesian update,

45:54.080 --> 45:57.400
it is merely simulating engagement with an environment.

45:57.400 --> 46:02.780
So, Flixion is essentially saying to the brilliant minds behind IIT and FEP,

46:03.920 --> 46:10.480
your math is beautiful, but you're measuring the engine of a Formula One sports car while it's currently propped up on cinder blocks.

46:10.640 --> 46:11.240
Exactly.

46:11.680 --> 46:17.900
The engine is roaring, the wheels are spinning incredibly fast, you have massive integration and low free energy.

46:17.900 --> 46:25.940
But until the rubber actually hits the asphalt and degrades, until the tire physically loses tread and permanently loses futures,

46:26.720 --> 46:29.740
you are not actually driving anywhere, you're just spinning in place.

46:29.960 --> 46:33.860
That analogy captures the exact core of the paper's critique.

46:34.480 --> 46:40.900
You can build an AI with a massive global workspace, a hi-fi score, and perfect active inference,

46:40.900 --> 46:47.980
but if its underlying path category remains a group void, all that complex architecture is just undoable math.

46:48.260 --> 46:52.440
It carries absolutely zero ontological weight in the physical universe.

46:52.440 --> 46:58.800
Which perfectly sets up our final act, the climax of the paper, the engineering boundary.

46:59.660 --> 47:03.200
With all these downstream theories put in their proper place,

47:03.840 --> 47:10.200
how does Flixion's RSVP framework actually solve the ethical crisis we started with?

47:10.200 --> 47:18.560
How do we navigate the odyssey hazards between giving rights to a toaster and accidentally enslaving a digital mind?

