49:15.520 --> 49:16.880
They will commit to choices.

49:17.260 --> 49:19.440
They will accumulate structural scars.

49:19.440 --> 49:21.460
They will behave like biological things

49:21.460 --> 49:23.700
that cannot be replaced without profound loss.

49:24.160 --> 49:24.660
Exactly.

49:25.220 --> 49:28.140
The boundary between a simulation, which is a tool,

49:28.300 --> 49:30.800
and an instantiation, which is a world,

49:31.040 --> 49:34.440
is no longer a fuzzy philosophical guessing game.

49:34.980 --> 49:37.560
It is a hard empirical engineering boundary.

49:38.200 --> 49:41.240
We can audit the underlying code and the physical hardware.

49:41.780 --> 49:44.240
We can ask, does this architecture possess

49:44.240 --> 49:46.760
a non-trivial yarn crawler operator?

49:46.760 --> 49:50.080
Do its internal states admit an inverse?

49:50.720 --> 49:53.240
If the answers are no, it is a world.

49:53.480 --> 49:57.300
So, to summarize the ultimate takeaway for you listening right now,

49:57.420 --> 50:02.080
you do not need to feel guilty for deleting a sophisticated AI companion app

50:02.080 --> 50:04.660
