That is going to stick with me for a very long time.

51:04.220 --> 51:10.880
But, um, if we take Fliction's theorem seriously to its absolute logical limit,

51:11.340 --> 51:15.260
it raises one final genuinely terrifying question.

51:15.380 --> 51:18.900
A question that flips this entire framework back onto humanity.

51:19.160 --> 51:19.800
Wait, what do you mean?

51:19.800 --> 51:26.580
Well, if worldhood, identity, and moral status are strictly defined by the irreversible loss

51:26.580 --> 51:32.520
of futures, by the accumulation of entropy, and the absolute inability to perfectly reconstruct

51:32.520 --> 51:35.900
the past, what happens to human beings in the future?

51:36.300 --> 51:42.920
What happens if biotechnology eventually succeeds in inventing perfectly reversible biological aging?

51:43.260 --> 51:49.480
What if we actually develop digital mind uploading that allows us to load safe states of our

51:49.480 --> 51:55.340
own neural architecture, allowing us to perfectly revert our brains to yesterday's state if we

51:55.340 --> 51:56.480
experience a trauma?

51:57.160 --> 51:58.080
Oh my god.

51:58.100 --> 52:03.780
If we successfully eliminate the thermodynamic loss of our own futures, if we technologically

52:03.780 --> 52:10.920
engineer ourselves to be perfectly, cleanly reversible, do we, under Fliction's theorem,

52:11.300 --> 52:14.500
mathematically engineer ourselves out of worldhood?

52:14.580 --> 52:15.340
Just, wow.

52:15.760 --> 52:18.640
Do we downgrade ourselves into mere tools?

52:18.640 --> 52:24.100
If we conquer death and irreversibility, we mathematically erase the very mechanism that

52:24.100 --> 52:25.000
makes us real?

52:25.220 --> 52:26.600
That is terrifying.

52:26.840 --> 52:31.540
Let that simmer in your own non-reversible, constrained-accumulating, entropy-generating

52:31.540 --> 52:32.680
brain for a while.

52:32.880 --> 52:38.000
Remember where we started today, looking at a murky x-ray of the mind, caught in a dizzying,

52:38.100 --> 52:38.820
endless debate?

52:39.260 --> 52:42.560
We might finally have the clear, mathematical picture we need.

52:42.560 --> 52:47.840
But the image it shows might require us to hold tightly to our own mortality just to remain

52:47.840 --> 52:48.220
real.

52:48.480 --> 52:50.720
Thanks for joining us on this deep dive.

